    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "expected_prediction",
      "value": "With the correct sech initial condition and SSFM at Δt=1e-4, N=1024, the L2 error at t=10 will be ≲1e-9 and the discrete Noether charge drift will be bounded (non-secular, oscillatory, amplitude ~1e-12), satisfying both the L2<1e-6 and energy rel.err<1e-8 criteria. With explicit RK4 at the same Δt, the L2 error at t=10 will exceed 1e-4 with secular linear-in-t growth in dN/dt and dP/dt (drift rate ~O(Δt^4) local but accumulated linearly), failing the criteria — confirming that discrete Noether drift, not local truncation, is the dominant error mechanism. The CN fixed-point will converge within 10 iterations but still show secular charge drift, decoupling inner-loop convergence from long-time fidelity."
    },
